From 7e5861b93edb8aa5d34cd363a1675fe6f1acf85c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jetson <jetson@orin-nano.tail52323b.ts.net>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:57:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] nv_attach: map lowering fixes after the final review
 (forwarding fails closed, 1532 adds global)

Review of c27412f4..1fee25d1 (three lenses, each finding then checked by
another agent). The forwarding findings are not reachable from llvmbpf's
output today; the 1532 one was (pt_hist, from 026f490f to 1fee25d1):
- forwarded_key read statements with every '.' line skipped and found block
  starts with a line-anchored label regex. It now reads the text before the
  call as statements with their leading labels and braces noted, and gives
  up at a label or brace between the store and the call (another path or
  scope), at any directive (a .loc glues to the next instruction), at a
  literal that is not plain decimal (PTX reads 0770 as octal), and when a
  store's state space does not match its base or the key pointer is not on
  the generic frame. Labels may start with '%'.
- A process whose model maps are 1532 only did not run the pass, so its adds
  stayed generic while the delivery reads through .global: the pass now
  runs for 1532 maps too (the wrapper's isspacep.global branch).
- Tests: the 1530 lookup block forwarded and loaded, bpf_main left to the
  helper, sum-map updates and deletes kept, guarded .global atomics and
  reductions, an unguarded reduction and a vector write as barriers, the
  register in a vector's second place, the whole 64-bit lookup; 17 cases.
Known cost: the pass rescans the body per query (lat_mmvq's module about
15 ms against 5 ms; quadratic in very large probes), at load only.
lat_mmvq's generated PTX is unchanged (41b5bf76...); pt_victim's five tools
exact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
